## In this guide

- [Access to Work](/support/work-and-study/access-to-work/): grants for equipment, travel and support workers
- [Disabled Students' Allowance](/support/work-and-study/disabled-students-allowance/): extra help for students in higher education

## Your rights at work

Under the **Equality Act 2010**, employers must not treat you unfairly because of a disability, and must make **reasonable adjustments**, such as changes to hours, equipment or duties. See the work pages in our guides to [health conditions](/conditions/) for examples for your condition.

## Help finding work

- **Jobcentre Plus** work coaches can refer you to specialist support.
- The **Disability Confident** scheme shows employers who have committed to recruiting and supporting disabled people.
- Many areas run **supported employment** programmes, and mental health services often offer **Individual Placement and Support** to help people into work.

## Carers who work

See [help for carers](/support/carers/) for your right to **carer's leave** and to ask for **flexible working**.
